# BinFlow M10 tier-matrix deviation whitelist (T-277, ADR-0032/0033 /
# architecture 15.6 — the T-250 discipline applied to the tier x addon plane).
#
# The M10 machine gate: scripts/m10-tier-matrix.sh --expect diffs every
# observed (form, row, status) cell against the frozen contract baseline in
# scripts/m10-tier-matrix.baseline (the m9-done opening posture: license and
# addons planes absent, pilot package types unknown, the disabled form's
# config key rejected by the strict YAML loader). Any mismatch fails the run
# — UNLESS the exact tuple is registered here first. M10 opens with an EMPTY
# registry: no deviation is pre-approved, which is the point. Landing tickets
# (FR-84/85/86...) flip cells deliberately; each flip gets its entry HERE,
# with the ticket/ADR reference, so the gate stays green while the change
# stays attributed.
#
# Entry format (one tuple per line; a trailing " # T-xxx/ADR-xxx: reason"
# comment is stripped before matching):
#
#   form|row|status   # T-xxx (ADR-xxx): why this flip is deliberate
#
# Rules:
#   - form: community | pro | enterprise | expired | disabled
#   - row: T01..T06 (see the script header for the row table)
#   - status: the OBSERVED code the entry tolerates (e.g. 200, 400, 403,
#     BOOTFAIL)
#   - an entry whose deviation stops happening is reported WL-STALE and still
#     fails the run — delete dead entries, do not let the registry rot
#   - rewriting the baseline itself is NOT done via this file: an ADR must
#     register the flip first, then scripts/m10-tier-matrix.sh --record
#     --force re-freezes it (per-milestone evolution)

# --- registered deviations -----------------------------------------------
# The license plane landing (T-279, ADR-0032 / §15.1.4): GET
# /api/system/license serves the effective state on every bootable form.
# The route landed with commit 90929f9; the flip stayed unregistered (a
# stale pre-T-279 bin/ binary masked it in the T-279 gate run) and is
# booked here by T-282's gate leg, which re-built the binary and re-ran
# the gate before touching anything.
community|T01|200   # T-279 (ADR-0032 §15.1.4): GET api/system/license landed (booked by T-282's gate leg)
pro|T01|200         # T-279 (ADR-0032 §15.1.4): GET api/system/license landed (booked by T-282's gate leg)
enterprise|T01|200  # T-279 (ADR-0032 §15.1.4): GET api/system/license landed (booked by T-282's gate leg)
expired|T01|200     # T-279 (ADR-0032 §15.1.4): GET api/system/license landed (booked by T-282's gate leg)

# The addon registry + status plane landing (T-282, ADR-0033 / §15.2.5):
# GET /api/v1/addons serves the slot manifest with live evaluation. The
# gated pilot rows T05/T06 are deliberately UNTOUCHED (still 400 — the
# slots are registered but adapterless; the gate weave is T-283 and the go
# adapter is T-285), so no entries for them.
community|T02|200   # T-282 (ADR-0033 §15.2.5): GET api/v1/addons landed (11-slot manifest, floor evaluation)
pro|T02|200         # T-282 (ADR-0033 §15.2.5): GET api/v1/addons landed (un-installed posture without --license-dir)
enterprise|T02|200  # T-282 (ADR-0033 §15.2.5): GET api/v1/addons landed (un-installed posture without --license-dir)
expired|T02|200     # T-282 (ADR-0033 §15.2.5): GET api/v1/addons landed (un-installed posture without --license-dir)
